{
    "background_story": "Dashing was a majestic stallion with a coat as rich and dark as the finest cocobolo wood. His owner, a skilled woodworker, had named him after the prized Central American hardwood, known for its beauty and strength. Dashing lived up to his name, with a shiny black coat and a spirited personality to match. He was a champion show jumper, with a talent for soaring over obstacles and a flair for the dramatic. But Dashing's true beauty lay in his gentle nature, earning him the love and admiration of everyone at the stable. When his owner fell ill, Dashing remained by his side, a constant and loyal companion, just as the durable cocobolo wood remains strong and resilient over time.",
